the Candyman according to legend if you  look into a mirror and chant his name  five times he will appear behind you and  his hook will be the last thing you ever  see but who is the Candyman the story  itself first appeared in 1890 after the  death of a painter in Chicago the  Candyman was the son of a slave who  became extremely wealthy when he  invented a machine that allowed him to  mass-produce shoes during the American  Civil War the man was able to send his  son to all of the best schools in  America and as a result he grew up to  become a good-natured gentleman and an  established painter the young man was  commissioned by a wealthy landowner to  paint his daughter  the painter fell in love of the land on  his daughter and they would eventually  have a child outside of wedlock when the  girl's father discovered their  relationship he was outraged  he hired a lynch mob to find and kill  the painter eventually they cornered the  painter in a barn and they cut off his  right hand of a rusty blade they smeared  his body with honey and watched as bee  stung him to death future generations of  the neighborhood old christened him the  Candyman the Candyman is a tower and six  foot five inches tall he wears a brown  fur trench coat a white cravat around  his neck grey pants and polished leather  shoes he has a bloody hook in place of  his right hand which he uses to mutilate  his victims the trench coat is used to  cover the grotesque mutilations he  suffered underneath it reveals he  skinless ribcage and he's hollowed out  abdomen he's organs infested by the bees  that live within him  in the second Candyman movie we find out  that his name is Daniel  sometime after his death Daniels ghost  rose from the grave and became a  vengeful spirit who will torment  anyone who dares to question his  existence his only goal was to keep the  stories and rumors surrounding his death  alive as he believed if people feared  him he would be able to continue  hunt the land and so the legend arose  anyone who shall recite the name  Candyman five times in the mirror then  immediately turn off the lights or  summon the ghosts who will slay all that  have witnessed its appearance the  Candyman is immortal and cannot be  killed by conventional means however it  is believed that there is a mirror that  contains his soul and is the source of  his power if the mirror is destroyed he  will cease to exist  if you've enjoyed this video then please  go ahead and leave it a like consider  subscribing if folklore mythology is  something that interests you if you have  anything you'd like to discuss or have  any ideas for future videos then please  go ahead and let me know in the comments  below as always I've been your host  mythology and folklore explained  [Music]
 

